  "_steam_comment": [
    "Steam entries use 'exec' instead of core/rom, e.g.:",
    "  { \"id\": \"celeste\", \"name\": \"Celeste\", \"system\": \"Steam\",",
    "    \"exec\": \"steam\", \"execArgs\": [\"-applaunch\", \"504230\"], \"layout\": \"nes\" }",
    "Requires: image built with --build-arg WITH_STEAM=1, and a ONE-TIME manual",
    "login performed by you (no account is created and no credentials are typed",
    "by the agent). Use a throwaway account with no payment method: account",
    "sharing breaks Steam's subscriber agreement, and a full keyboard reaches",
    "Steam's own settings."
  ],
  "_env_comment": [
    "Per-game `env` overrides. FNF (Lime/OpenFL) came up with working audio but a",
    "black window on this GPU-less box: the game loop ran and drove sound while its",
    "GL surface never reached the X window. These force Mesa's software path",
    "explicitly instead of letting the engine pick. RetroArch and Chromium do not",
    "need this \u2014 they have their own software fallbacks."
  ]
}
